@@ -4,6 +4,19 @@ The browser runs the original game. A loopback server routes JSON requests from
 
 The contract exposes player-level observations and actions so an agent can play through the normal game rules. Observations must not disclose hidden world state, and actions must retain native prerequisites, production queues, pathfinding, placement and combat resolution. A successful transport or queue receipt is not proof of a successful game action.
 
+## Scouting and neutral oil capture
+
+`observe.exploration` contains bounded `native-local-shroud` frontier samples near
+owned mobile units. Samples distinguish valid shrouded cells from revealed terrain;
+they do not expose hidden objects, guarantee passability, or represent a complete
+exploration map. A controller must track movement and abandon stalled destinations.
+
+`act` with `action: "capture"`, one owned visible engineer `unit`, and a visible
+neutral `CAOILD` `target` uses the native target-click decision path. It does not
+force ownership or bypass pathfinding. Other unit/target combinations are rejected.
+Confirm completion only when an observation lists the oil derrick as owned; a
+submitted receipt, missing engineer, or disappeared target is not capture proof.
+
